# Sazh Katzroy: "Whenever this creature attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature, then double the number of +1/+1 counters on
# that creature." Sazh is the only creature, so it is the lone target (no choice). On turn 3 it has none: one is added, then
# doubled, so it ends with two (a 5/5), not zero doubled. On turn 5 it has two: three after the counter, six after doubling (an
# 9/9) - counter first (2+1)*2 = 6, where doubling first would give 2*2+1 = 5.

